}

###
# modify addReview so it automatically links the logged‑in customer (instead of passing customerId manually)? That way reviews are always tied to the correct user session.

# Best Practice Refinements
# Authentication: If you want reviews tied to logged‑in customers, remove customerId from the mutation and instead resolve the customer from the ctx.activeUserId.

# Pagination: Add skip and take args to reviewsByProduct for scalability.

# Moderation: Add an Admin API mutation like deleteReview(id: ID!) for moderation.








### Add Review to product ID 38  OK OK OK
POST http://192.168.0.53:3000/shop-api
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "mutation AddReview($productId: ID!, $rating: Int!, $comment: String!) { addReview(productId: $productId, rating: $rating, comment: $comment) { id rating comment createdAt product { id name slug } customer { id firstName } } }",
  "variables": {
    "productId": "38",
    "rating": 5,
    "comment": "again --> Great product overall!"
  }
}

